s></name><name><surname>Doll</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Smoking, smoking cessation and lung cancer in the UK since 1950: combination of national statistics with two case&#x02013;control studies</article-title><source>BMJ</source><year>2000</year><volume>321</volume><fpage>323</fpage><lpage>329</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'BMJ||321|323||bib13|'--></citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-wrap><fig id="fig1"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>Types of cancer considered to be causally related to tobacco smoking in successive IARC monograph evaluations (<xref ref-type="other" rid="bib10">International Agency for Research on Cancer, 1986</xref>, <xref ref-type="other" rid="bib11">2004a</xref>).</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="jpeg" xlink:href="92-6602361f1"/></fig></floats-wrap></article>